{
  "_readme": [
    "Which Nightreign model becomes which L4D2 role.",
    "'source' lists files relative to your UNPACKED Nightreign game folder, e.g. \"chr/c1234.chrbnd.dcx\",",
    "or several part files (body/head/arms/legs) that get merged into one model.",
    "You can also point at an .fbx you exported yourself (Smithbox / FLVER editor).",
    "Leave 'source' empty to keep the vanilla L4D2 model for that role.",
    "Run 'python tools/melt.py scan' to list candidate files, and identify them in Smithbox's model viewer.",
    "'reference' is the L4D2 model whose skeleton, animations and hitboxes the converted model inherits.",
    "'rig': humanoid = auto-fit the mesh onto the L4D2 skeleton (best for people);",
    "       bone_map = only rename bones using 'bone_map' (for creatures you mapped by hand);",
    "       rigid    = glue the whole mesh to one bone (statue-like, last resort)."
  ],

